From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daryl Denson <9751141+denson9874@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 13:09:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] gs201: don't install LineageOS's 2022 AiAi association
 allowlist

allowlist_com.google.android.as.xml gives Private Compute Services
(com.google.android.as.oss) an allow-association list (only Android System
Intelligence). A package with any allow-association entry refuses
every package not listed, and stock cheetah (CP3A) has no such entry for it:
Google dropped that restriction, so here anything else that binds Private
Compute Services was refused. The file's rules for Android System
Intelligence itself are a subset of stock's, which vendor/gms installs
byte-identical. release-checks.sh flagged it once it had a stock dump.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 common.mk | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/common.mk b/common.mk
index 29e702aa..2aaafd6a 100644
--- a/common.mk
+++ b/common.mk
@@ -285,9 +285,9 @@ PRODUCT_COPY_FILES += \
 # Hardware Info
 include hardware/google/pixel/HardwareInfo/HardwareInfo.mk
 
-# AiAi Config
-PRODUCT_COPY_FILES += \
-    device/google/gs201/allowlist_com.google.android.as.xml:$(TARGET_COPY_OUT_PRODUCT)/etc/sysconfig/allowlist_com.google.android.as.xml
+# AiAi Config: not LineageOS's allowlist_com.google.android.as.xml. Stock's
+# association rules for Android System Intelligence come with vendor/gms, and
+# stock no longer restricts Private Compute Services (com.google.android.as.oss).
 
 # Android Verified Boot
 PRODUCT_COPY_FILES += \
-- 
